/** Tex's graph in words, as every Tex agent reads it (`texArchitecture.js`). */
export const TEX_MAP = "Tex is a graph of steps (nodes) joined by wires, both read from Tex's config (texConfig.json), which is what runs. A step is code or one model call. A wire says what runs next and on what: \"then\" runs the next step on this one's output, only when its condition holds; \"may call\" lets a step call another and wait for the answer; \"may send work back to\" returns a draft for another try; \"may start as a background job\" starts work that reports later; \"afterwards, in the background\" runs once the text has gone, with nobody waiting.\n\nA turn starts at one of: Check-in; Routine runs; Send through Tex; A text arrives.\n\n- Check-in (code, no model): Three times a day, look at what changed in their workspace, mail and calendar, and text them only what can't wait; most looks stay quiet. Runs the front door with its own read-only tools and setup model.\n  then: Front door\n- Routine runs (code, no model): Run a routine note under tex/routines/ on its schedule, as the person who wrote it, and text what it found unless it has nothing to say.\n  then: Read the text\n- Send through Tex (code, no model): Another AI connected to Context asks Tex to text the person (send notify) because something needs them now; their settings decide whether it goes, and it is texted as written, with no model.\n  then: Text them\n- A text arrives (code, no model): Take every text, picture or tapback from iMessage or WhatsApp and get it into the chat's record before anything decides about it.\n  then: Decide\n- Decide (Clef): Choose, from labelled examples, whether this text gets an answer, a reaction, a short wait or nothing, so Tex never answers what wasn't for it.\n  then: React; Queue\n- Queue (code, no model): Keep one turn per chat at a time (groups up to three side by side) so two answers never race each other.\n  then: Read the text\nDoor steps (a group of steps): Read the text, Run a routine, Check the question, Settle a yes or no, Watch what leaves, Check it may run, Read the history, Open the web, Read the setup, Bookkeeping, Prepare the answer.\n- Read the text (code, no model): Read the request: who is asking, from which chat, and what they asked.\n  then: Run a routine (when next); Text them (when answered)\n- Run a routine (code, no model): For a routine's run: reload the routine, and stop here when it is paused or its job needs no model.\n  then: Check the question (when next); Text them (when answered)\n- Check the question (code, no model): Check the question and what came with it: the files, the message it replies to, the tapbacks.\n  then: Settle a yes or no (when next); Text them (when answered)\n- Settle a yes or no (code, no model): A texted yes or no settles a waiting approval here, in code, before any model runs.\n  then: Watch what leaves (when next); Text them (when answered)\n- Watch what leaves (code, no model): Start this turn's egress ledger: what it reads from outside and what it may send out.\n  then: Check it may run (when next)\n- Check it may run (code, no model): Start reading the tools and the history, and check the model may run here.\n  then: Read the history (when next); Text them (when answered)\n- Read the history (code, no model): Hear voice messages, keep sent files, and read the chat's history and the tools offered.\n  then: Open the web (when next)\n- Open the web (code, no model): Pick the write tools for this chat and open the browser, vouched for by the person's own words.\n  then: Read the setup (when next)\n- Read the setup (code, no model): Read Tex's setup: its prompt, history length, skills, models, router and fallback.\n  then: Bookkeeping (when next)\n- Bookkeeping (code, no model): Prepare what the turn records: usage, the turn log, the ledger turn id, the pictures to keep.\n  then: Prepare the answer (when next)\n- Prepare the answer (code, no model): Start the side read of Tex's notes and set up the answer checks and pictures.\n  then: Front door; Router\n- Router (Clef, turned off: never runs): Send a plain lookup to a cheaper path and keep the front door for changes and thinking.\n  then: Front door\n- Front door (Haiku 5.5): Write Tex's answer: read the chat, call the tools that do the work, and draft the reply.\n  then: Answer checks\n  may call: Tools (when action); Advisor (when stuck); Fallback (when down); Big-ask planner (when big)\n  may start as a background job: Background job (when job)\n- Fallback (GLM-4.7 Flash): Answer when the front door's model is down, so a text never goes unanswered.\n- Big-ask planner (Opus 5.5, turned off: never runs): Break a big ask into steps before the front door starts, so it doesn't wander.\n- Tools (code, no model): Do the actual work in Context and the world: read, write, manage and send. Added only in code.\n  may call: Mail checker (when email); Card check (when card)\n- Advisor (Opus 5.5): Think harder when the front door is stuck, and say what to try next.\n- Answer checks (code, no model): Catch what code can prove wrong in a draft (a claim with no call behind it, a missing link) before a model looks.\n  then: Reply reviewer (when action); Text them\n  may send work back to: Front door\n- Mail checker (Haiku 5.5): Read an email before it goes and stop one that is wrong, rude or to the wrong person.\n- Card check (Haiku 5.5): Check a card's fields match what was asked before it is shown.\n- Reply reviewer (Haiku 5.5): Read the draft as the person would and send it back when it misses, so they never get a wrong or lazy answer.\n  then: Text them (when action)\n  may send work back to: Front door (when action)\n- Text them (code, no model): Deliver the answer: the texts, any card, and a reaction, as the chat's service allows.\n  afterwards, in the background, nobody waiting: Classifier; Self-review\n- React (code, no model): Put Decide's tapback on their text straight away, so a thanks or a win gets a reaction without a reply.\n- Classifier (Haiku 5.5): File each text into a conversation thread after the reply, so later turns see a short index instead of everything.\n- Self-review (Haiku 5.5): Look back at a sent answer and note what to do better next time.\n- Background job (Haiku 5.5): Do long work (browsing, forms, many steps) without holding up the reply.\n  may call: Tools (when job); Job check (when job); Advisor on job mail (when job)\n  may start as a background job: Hand-back judge (when job)\n- Job check (Opus 5.5): Check a job's work as it goes and steer it when it drifts.\n- Advisor on job mail (Opus 5.5): Decide what to tell the person when a job gets mail it can't handle alone.\n- Hand-back judge (Haiku 5.5): Make sure what a job hands back is true and finished before the person hears it.";
